---

<Base title="Women's Wellness IOP in CT | Hopewell Health Solutions" description="A trauma-informed Women's Wellness Intensive Outpatient Program at Hopewell Health Solutions, Glastonbury CT — DBT, EMDR & somatic therapy. Day & evening, 8–12 weeks. A program for women, by women." image={P + "group-room-bright.webp"}>
  <Header />
  <main class="hw">
    <ServiceHero
      crumbs={[{ label: "Programs", href: "/programs/" }, { label: "IOP", href: "/programs/intensive-outpatient-program/" }, { label: "Women's Wellness" }]}
      title="Women's Wellness Intensive Outpatient Program (IOP)"
      lede="Women's Wellness IOP · Glastonbury, CT · Day &amp; evening. A program for women, designed by women."
      bullets={heroUsps}
      facts={[{ icon: "star", text: "4.8 · 368 Google reviews" }, { icon: "pin", text: "Glastonbury & Westbrook" }]}
      image={P + "group-room-bright.webp"}
    >
      <p style="margin-top:18px;font-size:14.5px;color:#b9cbe0">Medically reviewed by <a class="inl" href="/provider/kristine-a-schlichting-ph-d/">Kristine Schlichting, PhD</a></p>
    </ServiceHero>
    <Creds />

    <Split heading="We understand the load women carry" img="/Assets/service/womens-wellness.webp" alt="Women supporting each other in Hopewell's Women's Wellness IOP" img2={P + "group-room-bright.webp"} alt2="A calm group room for the Women's Wellness IOP">
      <p><strong>A space to pause, process &amp; heal.</strong> Between work, parenting, caregiving, relationships, health concerns, and the constant pressure to “hold it all together,” it’s easy to lose your sense of self. That’s why we created the Women’s Wellness IOP — a supportive, structured space where women can pause, process, and begin to heal.</p>
      <p>This 8–12 week program is for women experiencing emotional burnout, <a class="inl" href="/what-we-treat/anxiety/">anxiety</a>, stress, life transitions, relationship challenges, low self-esteem, or the lingering effects of <a class="inl" href="/what-we-treat/trauma-ptsd/">trauma</a>. Whether you’re overwhelmed, disconnected, or simply ready to prioritize yourself — you don’t have to do it alone.</p>
    </Split>

    <section class="section is-mist">
      <div class="container">
        <div class="sec-head">
          <h2>Seeking care is a vital form of self-care</h2>
          <p class="lede">Why women’s mental health matters.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pg-stats" style="--n:3">
          {stats.map(([n, d]) => <div class="pg-stat"><strong>{n}</strong><span>{d}</span></div>)}
        </div>
        <p class="sec-foot">Irritability, emotional numbness, disrupted sleep, chronic stress, or difficulty in relationships can be signs of unresolved trauma or accumulated stress. These are treatable — and you deserve a space where healing is supported.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <Split heading="Is this program right for me?" img="/Assets/girl%20thinking%20worried.webp" alt="A woman reflecting on whether the Women's Wellness IOP is right for her" reverse>
      <p><strong>The space &amp; support you’ve been looking for.</strong> You may be so used to functioning on autopilot that you’ve stopped checking in with yourself. Consider:</p>
      <CheckList items={questions} icon="heart" />
      <p>If any of these resonate, this program may offer the space and support you’ve been looking for. <a class="inl" href="/admissions/">Take our quick screening</a>.</p>
    </Split>

    <section class="section is-stone">
      <div class="container pg-two">
        <div>
          <h2>What our program offers</h2>
          <p class="lede"><strong>More than just talk therapy.</strong> A trauma-informed, immersive experience designed to help women heal from past and ongoing trauma. You’ll engage in process-based group therapy, individual support, psychoeducation, and wellness activities — expressive arts, guided journaling, yoga-inspired movement, time in nature, somatic therapy, and animal-assisted support — to reconnect with your body, reduce stress, and rebuild trust.</p>
          <p class="lede">It’s grounded in evidence-based treatment: DBT, EMDR, somatic therapies, and Trauma-Focused CBT, with optional medication management, on-call services, and family involvement when helpful.</p>
          <CheckList items={includes} cols={2} />
        </div>
        <Schedule title="Flexible schedule" stat="3 h" note="a day · Monday–Thursday · 8–12 weeks" days={[3, 3, 3, 3, 0, 0, 0]} tone={1} icon="heart" tracks={[["Day", "9 AM–12 PM"], ["Evening", "5–8 PM"]]}>
          <p>Monday–Thursday, <strong>9 AM–12 PM</strong> or <strong>5–8 PM</strong> · 300 Hebron Ave, Suite 212, Glastonbury.</p>
        </Schedule>
      </div>
    </section>

    <IconCards heading="Even if you’re telling yourself…" lede="You deserve help." items={beliefs.map((b, i) => ({ icon: ["alert", "users", "clock", "shield"][i], t: b, d: "" }))} tone="white">
      <p class="sec-foot">You don’t have to wait until things get worse. Wellness isn’t about comparison — it’s about taking care of yourself because you’re worth it. You’ve carried a lot. You don’t have to carry it alone.</p>
    </IconCards>

    <Quote text="When we invest in women, we invest in our future." cite="Dr. Kristine Schlichting, Founder" img={P + "group-room-bright.webp"} />

    <ModalitiesOutcomes modalities={modalities} outcomes={outcomes} note="Plus <a class='inl' href='/programs/medication-management/'>medication management</a> &amp; additional <a class='inl' href='/treatment-methods/therapeutic-treatments/'>therapeutic treatments</a>." />

    <VideoCarousel videos={stories} heading="Women’s Wellness Stories, in Their Own Words" lede="Women who went through the program share what changed. More conversations on the <a class='inl' href='/podcast/'>Hope, Health &amp; Healing podcast</a>." />

    <NewsVideos heading="Trauma in women" lede="As seen on NBC Connecticut. Connecticut’s news outlets turn to our clinicians to talk about women’s mental health and trauma. Watch our team on CT Live! discuss why so many women carry trauma — and how the right support changes everything." videos={[{ id: "uDy-K1dO0Fw", t: "CT Live!: Trauma in Women — Hopewell Health Solutions", outlet: "NBC Connecticut" }]} />

    <IconCards heading="Care that sees the whole you" lede="Why Hopewell Health Solutions." items={whyHopewell} cols={2} tone="stone" />

    <MediaStrip bg="white" heading="Our clinicians, featured across Connecticut" />
    <Reviews heading="What Our IOP Clients Say" first={["Women’s Wellness IOP", "IOP"]} />
    <Team heading="A Woman-Led Care Team" lede="Compassionate, evidence-based care from clinicians who understand the load women carry. <a class='inl' href='/about-us/team/'>Meet our full team</a>." slugs={["teesha-huertas-lcsw", "christina-lindsay-pmhnp-bc-aprn", "linda-scillia-pmhnp-bc-aprn", "chelsey-micciche-lpc", "kaitlyn-czapiga-lmsw", "traci-schneider-maatc-lpc-a-atr-p", "dori-bessette-crail-lmft"]} tone="stone" />

    <Insurance heading="Most major insurance — TRICARE East accepted as PPO" lede="We accept most major insurances, and TRICARE East is accepted as a PPO plan. Many participants also qualify for <strong>Connecticut Paid Leave or FMLA</strong>. Our team verifies your benefits at no cost — before you commit to anything." tone="white" />
    <Locations heading="Our Locations" lede="The Women’s Wellness IOP is held at 300 Hebron Ave, Suite 212, Glastonbury (morning and evening), and at our Westbrook office, 70 Essex Road · plus virtual visits statewide. Reach us at <a class='inl' href='tel:8607351448'>(860) 735-1448</a> · <a class='inl' href='mailto:hhs4help@gmail.com'>hhs4help@gmail.com</a>." current="glastonbury-ct-2" />
    <Faq faqs={faqs} heading="Women’s Wellness IOP — common questions" tone="white" />
    <OtherPrograms current="/programs/womens-wellness-iop/" />
    <ClosingCta heading="Ready to take the first step?" lede="Prioritizing your mental health is one of the most powerful, loving choices you can make for yourself. If you’re ready to stop surviving and start healing, we’re here to help." image={P + "group-room-bright.webp"} />
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
